  "definition": "Dyspraxia refers to a group of cognitive disorders in which a person cannot carry out skills they had previously learned, even though the problem is not due to basic motor or sensory loss. Major forms include difficulty putting intended movements into action and difficulty mentally organizing the steps of an action.",
